}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"937bdc3e-55fa-4313-b80e-2201ca7862a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the ball of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " about ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["B_r(v) = {w : d(v, w) \[LessEqual] r}", "TI"],
 ", and its volume is ",
 StyleBox["V(r) = |B_r(v)|", "TI"],
 ". Position ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " of the profile is the radius ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] 1."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2accc201-8d53-412b-ac39-046bce74d7d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On a Riemannian manifold of dimension ",
 StyleBox["d", "TI"],
 " and scalar curvature ",
 StyleBox["R", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Vol B_r = \[Omega]_d r^d (1 \[Minus] R r\.b2 / (6(d + 2)) + O(r\
\:2074))", "TI"],
 ". The count on a graph is the observer's measurement of this volume: the \
exponent is the dimension and the correction the curvature. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["LogDifferenceQuotients"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/LogDifferenceQuotients", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a14a876d-13ff-48b1-af1b-dfef9f006181"],
 " reads the exponent off the profile, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["DimensionCurvatureFit"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DimensionCurvatureFit", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fdd6b770-f4d6-46a9-ad58-60f9b125234b"],
 " both numbers."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7d5c1f7f-1137-4311-80d3-0ab76c25280a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On a flat lattice the count is the volume of the ball of a norm, not of a \
round disk: ",
 StyleBox["2r\.b2 + 2r + 1", "TI"],
 " on the square grid, the \[ScriptL]\.b9 ball, and ",
 StyleBox["1 + 3r(r + 1)/2", "TI"],
 " on the hexagonal tiling. The path metric of a periodic graph converges to \
a polyhedral norm, and the volumes see that norm."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3da6049e-b0fa-43a5-a85a-f447be510aa6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A window past the eccentricity repeats ",
 StyleBox["V(e)", "TI"],
 ", the whole component, so that the profiles of several vertices have equal \
length and can be transposed. The list and ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "432e2a14-02b3-472b-89d9-649b9a8571bf"],
 " forms read every vertex off one distance matrix."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7f2d2269-2c0f-4beb-aee9-f07caedabb27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The count is a convention for the outermost layer. Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Measure\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d549269-d585-46a9-b83e-c3aac776462f"],
 ", with \[PartialD]",
 StyleBox["B_r", "TI"],
 " the vertices of the ball that have a neighbour outside it:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3b523f2a-8086-44a5-a334-789e6765ad36"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "21a49a1a-edb4-4949-b17a-a0a3616f05b7"], Cell["Value", "TableText",
